      "reviewer_name": "Anonymous",
      "rating": null,
      "title": "'Home Row' beware",
      "review_text": "There is a specific generation who knows how to type using \"home row\". Your fingers always reset back to the same place on the keyboard and typing is fast and seamless without ever having to hunt and peck for keys. This keyboard tried to change that. By moving a single key (backslash and whatever | is called) they made it so you had to move your right hand OFF of the home row to hit the enter key, and then reset. If you use a keyboard for typing, this keyboard is NOT for you. If you're a gamer and didn't even know there was more to a keyboard than WASD, carry on you'll be fine. I wouldn't pay more than $32 for this keyboard though, it feels very flimsy.",
